   "stem": {
      "text": "A curve is given in polar coordinates by \\( r = \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)} + 4 \\). Using a calculator, find the value of \\( \\frac{dy}{d\\theta} \\) at \\( \\theta = 0.9 \\), where \\( y = r\\sin\\theta \\). Show the setup for the calculation, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
